    "title": "Model 39",
    "manufacturer": "Peenemünde Army Research Center",
    "description": "A Thiel alcolox booster engine used on the A-4 Series B/V-2 missile. The Model 39b was an interim design, but went into production. Used 18 x 1.5 tonne thrust chambers that fed a common mixing chamber, as combustion instability issues of a single large injector were unable to be resolved. Work began 1936, testing in 1939, and mass production from 1943-1945.",
