    "title": "A-3",
    "manufacturer": "General Electric (GE)",
    "description": "A basic pump-fed booster engine developed as an improved version of the Hermes A-1 for the Hermes A-3 ballistic missile. Difficulties with development led the program being split into two parts, with the smaller A-3A testing the engine and guidance systems for the larger A-3B. Although it was evaluated for use by the US Army as the SSM-A-16, it was rejected due to poor performance and reliability.",
