  {
    "id": "EPEX",
    "title": "EPEX MPD Thruster",
    "manufacturer": "Mitsubishi Heavy Industries (三菱重工)",
    "description": "The EPEX (Electrical Propulsion Experiment) was a pulsed magnetoplasmadynamic thruster, tested on the Japanese Space Flyer Unit satellite in 1995. Although the Soviet Union experimented with MPD thrusters extensively, the Space Flyer Unit was the first spacecraft to use an MPD thruster as its main propulsion system.",
    "default_config": "EPEX",
