    "manufacturer": "National Aviation Engine Company (SNECMA)",
    "description": "The Atar 08/09 was a late-1950s redesign of the Atar 101, increasing thrust (creating the Atar 08) and adding an afterburner (creating the Atar 09). The Atar 09 powered the next generation of French jet aircraft, including the Cheetah C/D/E/R, Mirage III/IV, and Mirage F1.",
