  {
    "id": "RD200",
    "title": "RD-200",
    "manufacturer": "ОКБ-456 (Glushko)",
    "description": "The first multi-chamber engine developed by Glushko. After Glushko's attempts to scale up existing engines for what would become the R-7 resulted in unresolvable combustion instability (RD-105/106), Glushko instead combined multiple chambers of his ED-140 engine into one to increase thrust. The result, the RD-200, proved successful and, although it never flew, its design formed the basis of the RD-107/108 and RD-214.",
    "default_config": "RD-200",
